// Title: DLL Load By System Process From Suspicious Locations
// Sigma ID: 9e9a9002-56c4-40fd-9eff-e4b09bfa5f6c
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-07-17 | Modified: 2023-09-18
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1070
// Description: Detects when a system process (i.e. located in system32, syswow64, etc.) loads a DLL from a
//   suspicious location or a location with permissive permissions such as "C:\Users\Public"
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/hackerhouse-opensource/iscsicpl_bypassUAC (Idea)
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ed4273b30b6bba81f525a9ba136c2bcdb6d8ca95/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_susp_dll_load_system_process.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\" and (FolderPath startswith "C:\\Users\\Public\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\PerfLogs\\")
